{
  Game.Ram - TEK-R13, the Ram: the TEK machine of level 2's boss arena. A
  hull on two wheels that faces left and drives back and forth, backward
  when it goes right - only the bunker's hunt turns it round; a mast of
  three sections in a well on its roof, with a head on the top of it; an
  eye that lights when the machine wakes, and brake lamps that burn as it
  brakes. Its two exhausts smoke a little at rest and hard while it
  drives, the jet thrown back off the stern.

  The eye is its telegraph: lit, it breathes slowly, and it blinks fast
  only as a warning - while a head rises or the heads change. The head's
  lens winks once a second while the head is up and locked, and burns red
  before and through a burst.

  The entrance is the machine's own: the music before it fades out, it
  drives in from beyond the right edge in the silence and brakes at its
  mark, a breath, the eye lights, the mast rises with the hunter on top,
  and the head locks - the moment the boss track starts. A death replays
  it from the stop on: the machine stands at its mark, the mast rises and
  the track plays on.

  Its hull wears the TEK shield over its body: a bullet flares the
  honeycomb and does nothing. Any touch of the hull or a wheel wounds the
  hero and throws him off - but the machine drives behind the pads: a hero
  who stands on one is out of its way, and stays so while he is over it in
  the air, until he comes down onto the floor. The throw goes away from
  its middle - straight up when that side leaves him no room to the wall
  (the screen's edge), so a hero pinned at a wall goes up toward the low
  pad there - and a thrown hero is out of its way until he comes down.
  Come down inside the hull, he has a moment to walk out of it unhurt;
  once he is clear, or the moment is over, a touch is a touch again.

  After the lock it watches the hero. Low - on the road, or in a jump off
  it under the low pads, where it can crush him - it presses: a rev, and
  to the wall on his side at a run a little slower than his. Higher -
  on a pad - it is out of reach of the ram but not of the gun: the
  machine roams in short legs, keeping him in the barrel's sights, and the
  hunter fires. With no hero to watch it roams the whole floor, one leg in
  three to the far wall.

  The hunter: its barrel turns on the sleeve within its own half, from
  straight up to a little under level, and follows the hero; past the
  vertical the head turns by squashing across its socket and opening
  mirrored. A burst comes after the lens has burned red for a while, and
  a rest comes after the burst - something to see coming and a gap to
  get out of the way. It grows harder by the thirds of its lives: three
  shots where the hero stood; three where he will be if he keeps going;
  a hose of six that keeps following him.

  The targets are the hunter's eye - its lens - and the top of its head
  down to the lens, as the art draws it: a bullet that comes onto it from
  above or from the side. Bullets pass the mast, the barrel and the rest
  of the head - one that comes up through it meets the top from inside
  and flies on. Its lives show as a row of cells over the head:
  as the head locks the row lights cell by cell while the lens burns white
  - this is what has lives - and only then the first burst. The last of
  its lives blows the head up, the empty row fades; the
  empty mast sinks into the well, the eye blinks, and the next head - the
  sweeper - rises.

  The sweeper: four level barrels that do not tilt. The head rides the
  mast to the hero's row - never under its own roof - stops, its barrels
  redden, and it sweeps the row in a stream. A hero on the road is the
  ram's: the sweeper sinks to the bottom of its mast and sweeps the row
  just over his jump - the closed ceiling. By the thirds of its lives: one
  sweep; the fork - his row, then at once the row he is likely to jump
  to; the ladder - it rides the mast while it fires. The target is the
  whole barrel pack, but two honeycomb plates under it take every bullet
  that climbs: the floor does it no harm. Its last life does not blow it
  up at once. The gun falls silent and its barrels burn red, the eye
  blinks, the alarm of an arena rebuild sounds; the machine brakes to a
  stand, holds a moment, then backs off to the right wall - a hero in its
  way is touched as ever. Only there the head overloads: it heats from
  red to white, its bolts thicken - then bursts with a white flash and a
  heavier jolt than the hunter's. A shock wave runs out of the burst over
  the whole screen in about a second - a dark band behind a thin white
  front, dust kicked up where it runs along the road - and throws the
  hero clear, as a touch of the hull does but with no wound: away from
  the hull, or from over it toward the side with more road - and with the
  hull at the wall that is always the left: the chase that follows starts
  from there; come down inside the hull, he walks out of it as after any
  throw. The empty mast sinks and the machine stands at the wall.

  The bunker: an armoured dome low on the mast, its barrels short, its
  hatch on top. It rises and lights its row; a breath after the row is
  lit the machine drives off and the chase begins: it does not leave the
  screen, the road slides under it (Game.Belt). It stands at the right
  wall and turns to the hero as the others do. Its hatch breathes: shut,
  it aims, and lobs a shell at where his feet are (Game.Shells); a beat,
  then a column of hot exhaust goes straight up out of the open hatch -
  it wounds whoever is in it; then the hatch stands open and cooling,
  and shuts. Its top is open to a bullet at any time: the dome as the
  art draws it down to a row of cells under the hatch, and the lid shut,
  open or on its way. One that comes down onto it steeply enough, from
  above or aslant from a pad, takes a life; a shallow one only flares the
  honeycomb. The honeycomb closes its sides and front under that row. Its
  lives go by thirds as the others' do.

  In its middle third comes its second phase. Now and then, its
  hatch shut, the eye blinks the warning and the machine lunges back to
  the middle of the screen - never to the left edge, where the hero could
  have nowhere to jump - stands a breath and drives back to the wall. A
  touch is a touch as ever. From the warning till it stands at the
  middle the bunker holds its fire; the road it leaves behind its stern
  is not the hero's: one who comes down onto it is thrown back over the
  hull to the left, with a wound. A hero on a pad is carried over it by
  the pad. Its shells come in pairs: one at his feet, one at the pad he
  stands on, or at one he could climb to once it has ridden past the
  middle of the screen - a pad is let in first, so the way up is caught
  on the right half - or onto the road ahead of him (Game.Shells).

  Its last third is the hunt. The fire stops, the eye blinks and the
  alarm sounds, and the game sends in a wave of pads, three rows of them;
  once they are in, the machine drives left through the hero and on off
  the screen, silent on the way. A hero up on the wave jumps over it. One
  left on the road is thrown up over the hull to the right with a wound -
  either way he ends right of it. Past the left edge it turns round,
  unseen but for the rumble and, before it comes back, its eye's red at
  the edge; then it drives in again bow first and hunts him. The right is
  his; the left is the machine's: its bow keeps a step behind him, as
  fast as he runs against the road, but within the left half. Now and
  then, after the eye's warning, it surges toward nearly the right edge
  for a couple of seconds and goes back as fast - a press, never a trap.
  It goes back for a hero only when he has come down behind its stern -
  one up on a pad it lets the road carry back over its hatch, where he
  strikes down. Any touch on the
  road is a ram: he is thrown up over the hull to the right with a wound -
  its bow never reaches the right wall, so there is always room - and it
  stands while he flies clear. Its shells come one at a time, a little
  more often than before: at the pad he stands on, which goes; in the air
  or on the road, at the road near him where no pad is in the way
  (Game.Shells finds it), so fewer pads are knocked away.

  The hull is drawn facing left; turned round, everything on it - the
  well and the mast, the eye, the lamps, the exhausts, its honeycomb,
  what a touch meets - is mirrored about its middle. The heads turn on
  their own.

  Its last life blows it up as the hunter's does; the empty mast sinks,
  and the machine runs on - the hunt with no head, its shells gone,
  nothing left on it to hit - till the hero's henshin. Killed before its
  last third (the debug key), it begins the hunt there.

  At the henshin the game brakes it: down to a stand by its brake, the
  lamps burning, and the hiss and the jolt as it stops. Then it stands
  with its eye lit, and nothing of it wounds or throws; a hero caught in
  the hull the game sets out of it. The burst at the end of the henshin
  throws it half a cell away from the hero and stuns it: its eye catches
  and drops out of step, its lamps go out, smoke comes out of its wheel
  arches. Stunned, it stands as harmless as before - and drives off at
  once, slow, faster, slow, to where the game wants it for the throw. As
  the pads spin up against it its lamps and its eye blink in alarm, the
  faster the more they spin; its honeycomb holds still.

  Its armour gone, the game breaks its front wheel off - the one on the
  side it faces. The wheel hops off, bounces lower and lower, every strike
  of the road in sparks, and rolls away to the right (Game.Wheel); the
  hull drops on that side about its rear wheel, the point of its plough
  digging into the road and scraping it in sparks.
  From then on a touch of the hull wounds and throws again. The bare hull
  and the wheel throw bullets off as a tank's armour does, and lose
  nothing to them.
  Then the game has it take off (Game.Takeoff): its engine bays come out
  of the depth of both arches - the rear one behind its wheel - and their
  nozzles slide down out of the rings, as far as the road lets them; fire
  out of the front nozzle lifts the bow, the rear jet catches and the hull
  rises on its two jets; a little way up the rear jet throws the rear
  wheel down to bounce and roll after the first, and the hull rights
  itself and hangs - bobbing, rocking, keeping over the hero with a lag.
  The engine is done with: its exhausts smoke no more from the takeoff on.
  Off the road it is where its pose puts it - turned, raised - and its
  touch, the bullets it throws off and everything drawn on it go with the
  pose. Once the bunker is gone and the mast has sunk, a hatch slides
  shut over the well, and the smoke out of it stops. The fire is short and
  narrow, a white-blue core in an orange sheath, gone well over the road;
  only its warmth reaches the road, and it lights the nozzle from below.

  A shed wheel leaves its arch hollow - a bullet and a touch go into it -
  till the bay comes out and fills it.

  Under half its lives either head shorts out: small bolts over it, the
  more often the fewer lives are left. The hunter smokes too at its last
  third.

  As either head's lives pass into their next third the machine tells it:
  the shuttle pays for a third with a medkit, two a head.

  TRam is the rules; TRamPainter draws them with TRamArt. The game carries
  out the cue of a tick: the sounds, the shake and the boss track, and the
  wound and the throw of a touch.

  Moon 2D remake. Requires Delphi 10.3+ (inline var).
}
unit Game.Ram;
{$I ..\Moon2D.inc}

interface

uses
  Sdl2.Core, Render.Brush, Render.Sprites, Sprites.Sets, Levels.Events,
  Levels.Dynamics, Monsters.Defs, Monsters.Hull, Game.Shield, Game.Wheel,
  Game.Takeoff, Effects.Sparks;

const
  RamWidth = 169.0;
  RamHeight = 128.0;
  // The road of the boss arena: the top of row 11
  RamFloorY = 352.0;
  RamTop = RamFloorY - RamHeight;
  // The hunter's eye on the first grade; the game scales them by its own
  HunterLives = 100;
  SweeperLives = 140;
  BunkerLives = 150;
  // Units a tick, as TBurst.NewBullet takes them
  HunterBulletSpeed = 6;
  SweeperBulletSpeed = 5;
  // The head's row of lives: three thirds of four cells
  HeadRowCells = 12;

type
  // rpWaiting - the music fades out, the machine is not on the screen yet;
  // rpBreathing - stopped at the mark of the entrance, the eye still dark;
  // rpRevving - the engine roars before it presses the hero; rpChanging -
  // a head is dead: the empty mast sinks and the next head rises
  TRamPhase = (rpAbsent, rpWaiting, rpDriving, rpBreathing, rpRising,
    rpResting, rpRevving, rpChanging);

  TRamHead = (rhNone, rhHunter, rhSweeper, rhBunker);

  // The bunker's breath: shut and aiming; shut, the shell just out; the
  // column of exhaust out of the open hatch; open and cooling - the window
  TBunkerHatch = (bhAiming, bhFired, bhVenting, bhOpen);

  // The bunker's second phase at the wall: waiting for the next fall
  // back; the eye's warning; the lunge to the middle; the stand there; the
  // drive back to the wall
  TFallBack = (fbNone, fbWarning, fbLunging, fbStanding, fbReturning);

  // The bunker's last third: none yet; the change - the wave called in,
  // the eye's warning; the pass through the hero off the left edge; the
  // turn round out there; the drive in again; the hunt, bow first; at the
  // henshin, the brake and the stand after it; thrown by its burst and
  // stunned
  TBunkerHunt = (htNone, htCalling, htPassing, htTurning, htEntering,
    htHunting, htBraking, htHalted, htStunned);

  // The hunt's surge toward the right edge: waiting for the next; the
  // eye's warning; the surge, then back to the left half
  THuntSurge = (hsWaiting, hsWarning, hsSurging);

  // The gun: idle (aiming or riding, resting), the warning before a burst
  // - the hunter's lens, the sweeper's barrels burning red - the burst
  TRamFire = (rfIdle, rfFlare, rfBurst);

  // The head's row of lives as the HUD draws it
  TRamRow = record
    // A head up, or one blown up a moment ago
    Shown: Boolean;
    // Cells lit so far as the row comes up after the lock
    Lit: Integer;
    // Lives left of the full
    Share: Single;
    // Ticks since the eye was last struck
    HitTicks: Integer;
    // 1, going to 0 as the row of a dead head fades
    Fade: Single;
  end;

  // What the machine sees of the hero this tick
  // The shock wave of the sweeper's blast: its front runs out at an even
  // pace to the farthest corner of the screen and is gone
  TShockWave = record
    // How far the front runs, units
    Reach: Single;
    // Ticks since the blast; below 0 - no wave
    Ticks: Integer;
    // The hero has been thrown by it
    Threw: Boolean;
    // From AFrom, the front at nothing
    procedure Start(const AFrom: TSdlFPoint);
    procedure Stop;
    procedure Tick;
    function Running: Boolean;
    // The front ATicks after the blast, units from it
    function FrontOf(ATicks: Single): Single;
  end;

  // The drive off after the henshin's burst: asked for; where its left
  // edge set off from and stands at the end; how long it takes and how
  // far along it is
  TRamWithdraw = record
    Asked: Boolean;
    From, Till: Single;
    Ticks, Clock: Integer;
  end;

  // A throw over the hull: to Side, Way units a tick across of its own on
  // top of his
  TOverTheHull = record
    Side: Integer;
    Way: Single;
  end;

  TRamTarget = record
    Alive: Boolean;
    Body: TSdlFRect;
    // Stands on a pad
    OnDeck: Boolean;
    // Where the second shell of a pair goes (SecondShellMark)
    SecondAt: TSdlFPoint;
  end;

  TRamCue = record
    // The engine runs: the rumble loops from now on
    Rumble: Boolean;
    // It has stopped: the rumble cuts to the brake's hiss
    Hiss: Boolean;
    // The mast starts up
    Whine: Boolean;
    // The head has locked at its height: the boss track
    Locked: Boolean;
    // A shake, in trauma shares; 0 - none
    Jolt: Single;
    // The head fires a bullet from ShotFrom along ShotAngle, degrees
    // counter-clockwise from the right, at ShotSpeed
    Shot: Boolean;
    ShotFrom: TSdlFPoint;
    ShotAngle: Integer;
    ShotSpeed: Integer;
    // The head has lost its last life: it blows up at BlastAt
    Blast: Boolean;
    BlastAt: TSdlFPoint;
    // The blast is the sweeper's: an overload, not a hit - the low blow,
    // the flash, and the shock wave it sends out
    Shock: Boolean;
    // One more cell of the head's row lit
    RowCell: Boolean;
    // The sweeper backs off to the wall: the alarm of an arena rebuild
    Alarm: Boolean;
    // The head's lives have passed into their next third
    Third: Boolean;
    // It drives off: the chase begins, the road slides under it
    Chase: Boolean;
    // The bunker lobs a shell out of LobFrom that comes down on LobAt
    Lob: Boolean;
    LobFrom, LobAt: TSdlFPoint;
    // In the hunt, he is not on a pad: the shell is for the road near LobAt,
    // where no pad is in its way - the game knows the decks
    LobForRoad: Boolean;
    // With it, in the second phase, a second shell out of the other muzzle
    SecondLob: Boolean;
    SecondLobFrom, SecondLobAt: TSdlFPoint;
    // The column of exhaust goes up out of the bunker's hatch
    Vent: Boolean;
    // Its last third: the rows of the hunt are to ride in
    Rows: Boolean;
    // A wheel it has shed strikes the road hard enough to be heard
    WheelLands: Boolean;
    // A jet catches in a well: the fire bursts out of it
    Ignite: Boolean;
    // Off the road: its jets roar from now on, in place of the rumble
    Hover: Boolean;
  end;

  // Where the hull stands and how: upright on the road with its left edge
  // at Left, turned Lean degrees clockwise about its rear wheel's touch of
  // the road, then moved by Shift
  TRamPose = record
    Left, Lean: Single;
    Shift: TSdlFPoint;
    function Upright: Boolean;
  end;

  TRam = class
  private
    FBody: TShieldMask;
    FWells: TShieldMask;
    FShield: TTekShield;
    FOrders: TRamOrders;
    FEntered: Boolean; // the whole entrance has begun on this level
    FPhase: TRamPhase;
    FPhaseTicks: Integer;
    FEntering: Boolean; // the drive under way is the entrance
    FAge: Integer;
    FX, FLastX: Single; // the hull's left edge, screen units
    FSpeed: Single; // units a tick, below 0 to the left
    FAccel: Single; // the change of the speed this tick
    FCruise: Single;
    FTarget: Single;
    FBraking: Boolean;
    FMast, FLastMast: Single;
    FSway, FLastSway: Single; // degrees clockwise
    FSwaySpeed: Single;
    FLamps, FLastLamps: Single;
    FLampHold: Integer;
    FEyeLit: Boolean;
    FEye, FLastEye: Single;
    FBreathTicks: Integer;
    FArmed: Boolean; // the head is up and locked
    FArmedTicks: Integer;
    FLens, FLastLens: Single;
    FHeroInFront: Boolean;
    FHeroThrown: Boolean; // flying from a throw: out of its way till he lands
    // Thrown, by a touch or the wave: ticks left to walk out of the hull
    // unhurt, if he comes down inside it
    FClearTicks: Integer;
    FArrivals: Integer;
    FDice: TXorShift;
    FCue: TRamCue;
    // The hero as it sees him, and how he moves: units a tick, smoothed
    FHero: TRamTarget;
    FHeroSeen: Boolean;
    FHeroCenter: TSdlFPoint;
    FHeroPace: TSdlFPoint;
    // Pressing a hero low on the road; the ticks that decide it
    FPressing: Boolean;
    FLowTicks, FAboveTicks, FDeckTicks: Integer;
    // The head, its lives and its facing: -1 left, as the art is drawn
    FHead: TRamHead;
    FLives, FFullLives: Integer;
    FLivesShare: Single; // the grade's
    FThirds: Integer; // the thirds of the head's lives told so far
    FHeadKilled: Boolean; // the last life is gone; it blows up next tick
    FKilled: TRamHead; // the head the change of heads began with
    FChangePending: Boolean; // braking to stand for the change of heads
    FChangeFrom: Single; // the mast's height as the change began
    FFacing: Integer;
    FTurnTicks: Integer; // a turn of the head under way, ticks left
    FPastTicks: Integer; // the hero has stood past the vertical
    // The barrel: its angle before the sway, degrees counter-clockwise from
    // the right, and the one it wants
    FAim, FLastAim: Single;
    FWant: Single;
    FInSights: Boolean; // the hero is within the barrel's half
    FFire: TRamFire;
    FFireTicks: Integer;
    FShotsLeft: Integer;
    // Where a burst goes, held from the moment the lens lights
    FFrozenAt: TSdlFPoint;
    FLensHot: Boolean;
    FHurtTicks: Integer;
    // The row of lives: ticks since the lock (-1 - none), since the last
    // hit, since the blast (-1 - none)
    FRowTicks: Integer;
    FHitTicks: Integer;
    FGoneTicks: Integer;
    // The sweeper: the row its barrels go to and sweep, a sweep of the
    // fork still to come, the way a ladder rides, the barrel that fires
    // next, how red the barrels burn
    FRowY: Single;
    FForkLeft: Boolean;
    FLadderWay: Integer;
    FNextBarrel: Integer;
    FHeat, FLastHeat: Single;
    FHeatTicks: Integer; // the whole of the burning before this sweep
    FPlates: array [0..1] of TTekShield;
    // The sweeper's last life gone: backing off to the right wall, ticks
    // since, ticks it has stood before the drive
    FRetreating: Boolean;
    FRetreatTicks: Integer;
    FStoodTicks: Integer;
    // The bunker up, it has driven off into the chase
    FChased: Boolean;
    // The bunker's breath, ticks left of it; how open the lid stands, 1
    // open; the muzzle that fires next; the honeycomb about it
    FHatch: TBunkerHatch;
    FHatchTicks: Integer;
    FLid, FLastLid: Single;
    // The hatch over the empty well, 0 open to 1 shut: it shuts once the
    // bunker is gone and the mast has sunk
    FShutter, FLastShutter: Single;
    FShutting: Boolean;
    FNextMuzzle: Integer;
    FHeadShield: TTekShield;
    // Its second phase: the step of a fall back, ticks into the step, and
    // ticks till the next one
    FFallBack: TFallBack;
    FFallBackTicks: Integer;
    FFallBackWait: Integer;
    // Its last third: the step of the hunt and ticks into it, the wave in,
    // and ticks it stands after a ram
    FHunt: TBunkerHunt;
    FHuntTicks: Integer;
    FRowsIn: Boolean;
    FRamStandTicks: Integer;
    // Thrown by the burst: where it stood and which way it goes, -1 left;
    // ticks the stunned eye holds its level yet
    FStunFrom: Single;
    FStunSide: Integer;
    FWithdraw: TRamWithdraw;
    // How strong the alarm of its lights is, and how far into its blinks
    FLightsAlarm: Single;
    FAlarmPhase: Single;
    FFlickerTicks: Integer;
    // The way the hull faces: -1 left, as the art is drawn
    FHullFacing: Integer;
    // Its front wheel off: ticks since; how far the hull leans, degrees
    // clockwise; the wheel on its way
    FShed: Boolean;
    FShedTicks: Integer;
    FLean, FLastLean: Single;
    FWheel: TLooseWheel;
    // Off the road on its jets; its rear wheel spat out on its way
    FTakeoff: TTakeoff;
    FRearWheel: TLooseWheel;
    // Ticks since the bare hull or its wheel last threw a bullet off
    FHullHitTicks: Integer;
    // The hunt's surge, and the ticks of its step - left of the wait,
    // into the warning or the surge
    FSurge: THuntSurge;
    FSurgeTicks: Integer;
    // Then: ticks of its overload so far
    FOverloadTicks: Integer;
    // The white of the sweeper's blast, 1 the tick it bursts, and where
    FFlash, FLastFlash: Single;
    FBlastAt: TSdlFPoint;
    FWave: TShockWave;
    procedure TickKill;
    procedure TickThirds;
    procedure BeginRetreat;
    procedure TickRetreat;
    function AtTheWall: Boolean;
    procedure TickChaseStart;
    procedure LockBunker;
    procedure TickBunkerTurn;
    procedure TickHatch;
    procedure TickLid;
    procedure Lob;
    function BunkerMuzzle(AIndex: Integer): TSdlFPoint;
    function BunkerMiddle: TSdlFPoint;
    function BunkerSecondPhase: Boolean;
    procedure TickFallBack;
    function HoldsFire: Boolean;
    function NextFallBackWait: Integer;
    function BunkerThirdPhase: Boolean;
    procedure BeginHunt;
    procedure TickHunt;
    procedure TickHuntDrive;
    procedure BeginTurn;
    function HuntMark: Single;
    procedure TickSurge;
    procedure TickBrake;
    procedure TickStun;
    procedure TickWithdraw;
    procedure TickShed;
    // Its strike of the road, if it struck, told and felt
    procedure HearStrike(const AWheel: TLooseWheel);
    procedure TickTakeoff;
    procedure SpitWheel;
    procedure TickShutter;
    function UprightBox(const ABox: TSdlFRect): TSdlFRect;
    function AlarmLight: Single;
    procedure FlickerEye;
    function HuntLine: Single;
    function NextSurgeWait: Integer;
    function SurgeWarns: Boolean;
    function SolidAt(ACol, ARow: Integer): Boolean;
    function WellOpen(AArtCol: Integer): Boolean;
    function WaveSide(const AHeroBody: TSdlFRect): Integer;
    procedure Place(AX: Single);
    procedure Arm(ALivesShare: Single);
    procedure BeginDrive(ATarget, ACruise: Single; AEntering: Boolean);
    procedure BeginRest(ATicks: Integer);
    procedure BeginLeg;
    procedure BeginPatrolLeg;
    procedure BeginHuntLeg;
    procedure BeginRev;
    procedure BeginChange;
    procedure SeeHero(const ATarget: TRamTarget);
    procedure TickMode;
    procedure PressNow;
    function PressWall: Single;
    function StopAhead: Single;
    function InSightsFrom(ALeft: Single): Boolean;
    procedure KillHead;
    procedure TickPhase;
    procedure TickChange;
    procedure TickDrive;
    procedure Arrive(AOldSpeed: Single);
    procedure TickSway;
    procedure TickAim;
    procedure TickRide;
    procedure TickFire;
    procedure TickSweep;
    procedure BeginSweep(AFlareTicks: Integer);
    function ForkRow: Single;
    procedure Shoot;
    procedure ShootBarrel;
    procedure TickHeat;
    procedure LockSweeper;
    function SweeperMastFor(ARowY: Single): Single;
    function SweeperRowY(AMast: Single): Single;
    function ToHead(const APoint: TSdlFPoint): TSdlFPoint;
    function EyeShare(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AShare: Single): Boolean;
    function TopShare(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AShare: Single): Boolean;
    function TopLine: Single;
    function InTop(const ALocal: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    function InDome(const ALocal: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    function InLid(const ALocal: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    function Tier: Integer;
    function CanShoot: Boolean;
    procedure TickRow;
    function RowLit: Integer;
    procedure TickLamps;
    procedure TickEye;
    procedure TickLens;
    function Overlaps(const ABox: TSdlFRect): Boolean;
    function SpanAcross(const ABox: TSdlFRect; out AFirst,
      ALast: Integer): Boolean;
    function ThrowSide(const AHeroBody: TSdlFRect): Integer;
  public
    // ABody - the hull and the wheels on a grid of units (TRamArt.Body);
    // AWells - the cells of it that are the wheels and the dark of their
    // arches (TRamArt.Wells), hollow while a wheel is gone and no bay has
    // come out in its place. Without them the wells stay solid.
    constructor Create(const ABody: TShieldMask; ASeed: Cardinal); overload;
    constructor Create(const ABody, AWells: TShieldMask;
      ASeed: Cardinal); overload;
    destructor Destroy; override;
    // Comes onto the screen as AOrders say: the whole entrance the first
    // time on the level - True, and the music must go silent - from the
    // stop on after that. The hunter comes with HunterLives times
    // ALivesShare.
    function Start(const AOrders: TRamOrders; ALivesShare: Single = 1): Boolean;
    // Back past the bunker's death, as a restart there asks: entered, the
    // mast empty, turning round beyond the left edge to come in bow first
    // and hunt, its eye's warning first
    procedure StartPastBunker(const AOrders: TRamOrders);
    // Back in the air phase, as a restart there asks: the honeycomb and
    // both wheels gone, the hull hanging level on its jets with its middle
    // over AMiddleX, facing right, keeping over the hero from now on
    procedure StartHanging(const AOrders: TRamOrders; AMiddleX: Single);
    // Gone from the screen: a door, a death
    procedure Clear;
    // A new level: gone, and the entrance not seen
    procedure Reset;
    function Tick(const ATarget: TRamTarget): TRamCue; overload;
    // No hero to watch: it roams and holds its fire
    function Tick: TRamCue; overload;
    // Where a bullet's stretch of this tick first meets the shield, which
    // flares there; False when it meets nothing
    function Block(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AAt: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    // A pad of the throw met the shield at AAt, a point of the screen: a
    // piece of it breaks off there
    procedure ShatterShield(const AAt: TSdlFPoint);
    // Where a bullet's stretch of this tick meets the hunter's eye or the
    // top of its head, which loses a life; False when it misses
    function StrikeHunter(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AAt: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    // Where a bullet's stretch of this tick meets the sweeper's barrel
    // pack: AGuarded - a climbing bullet, taken by a plate under it, which
    // flares; otherwise the pack loses a life. False when it misses.
    function StrikeBarrels(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AAt: TSdlFPoint;
      out AGuarded: Boolean): Boolean;
    // The hunter's lens on the screen now
    function LensPoint: TSdlFPoint;
    // The middle of the sweeper's barrel pack on the screen now
    function BarrelsPoint: TSdlFPoint;
    // Where a bullet's stretch of this tick meets the bunker: on its top,
    // falling steeply enough - a life; a shallow one, or the honeycomb
    // under the top, takes it, AGuarded, and flares. False when it misses.
    function StrikeBunker(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AAt: TSdlFPoint;
      out AGuarded: Boolean): Boolean;
    // The middle of the bunker's hatch on the screen now
    function HatchPoint: TSdlFPoint;
    // Under the hatch, where the honeycomb begins: over this line the top
    // takes a bullet, under it the honeycomb
    function OpenTop: TSdlFPoint;
    // The column of exhaust over the hatch holds some of ABody
    function ColumnHolds(const ABody: TSdlFRect): Boolean;
    // How open the bunker's lid stands, 0 shut to 1 open, between two ticks
    function LidAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    // A third of the lives of the head on the mast at once: the debug key's
    // way past a head
    procedure WoundThird;
    // The hero's body touches the hull or a wheel and he is in the
    // machine's way: AOnDeck - he stands on a pad, AInAir - on his way up
    // or down. AAway - the side to throw him to, away from its middle; 0 -
    // straight up, pinned against a wall. A thrown hero who comes down
    // inside the hull is out of its way until he is clear of it, for
    // ClearTicks at most.
    function Contact(const AHeroBody: TSdlFRect; AOnDeck, AInAir: Boolean;
      out AAway: Integer): Boolean;
    // He is to be thrown over the hull as AThrow says, and is out of its
    // way till he comes down. Falling back, he has come down onto the road
    // right of it (AOnRoad - not in the air, not on a pad): back to the
    // left. From the pass on, touched on the road: over it to the right.
    function ThrowsOverTheHull(const AHeroBody: TSdlFRect; AOnRoad: Boolean;
      out AThrow: TOverTheHull): Boolean;
    // Away from the right wall in a fall back: on its way, standing, or on
    // its way back - the napalm waits
    function FallingBack: Boolean;
    // In its last third: no fall back, the mortar folded - the machine
    // behind him is the leash
    function Hunts: Boolean;
    property Hunt: TBunkerHunt read FHunt;
    // The wave of the hunt has flown in: the pass may begin
    procedure RowsArrived;
    // Whole on the screen in its hunt: the henshin may brake it
    function CanBrake: Boolean;
    // Down to a stand, and standing from then on; nothing for one that
    // cannot brake
    procedure BrakeToAStand;
    // Braking or standing for the henshin, or stunned by its burst:
    // nothing of it wounds or throws
    function Halted: Boolean;
    // The burst of the henshin out of AFrom: thrown away from it half a
    // cell, stern first when it comes out of the middle, and stunned from
    // then on; nothing for one not braking or standing
    procedure Stun(const AFrom: TSdlFPoint);
    function Stunned: Boolean;
    // Stunned, its lamps and its eye blink together in alarm, ALevel 0
    // none to 1 - the faster the higher: the pads spun up against it at
    // the throw. A stun starts with none.
    procedure LightsAlarm(ALevel: Single);
    // Stunned, it drives off as soon as its throw is over, to stand with
    // its left edge at ALeft; nothing for one not stunned
    procedure Withdraw(ALeft: Single);
    // Stunned, its armour gone: the front wheel - the one on the side it
    // faces - breaks off, hops and rolls away to the right; the hull drops
    // on that side about its rear wheel, its nose scraping the road, and
    // from now on its touch wounds and throws again. Once a fight.
    procedure ShedWheel;
    function WheelShed: Boolean;
    property Wheel: TLooseWheel read FWheel;
    // Its front wheel shed, it takes off: the bays and the nozzles out,
    // the fire out of the front nozzle, the bow up, the rear wheel spat
    // out to roll after the first - the cue tells it - and up on both jets
    // to hang. Once a fight.
    procedure TakeOff;
    property Flight: TTakeoff read FTakeoff;
    property RearWheel: TLooseWheel read FRearWheel;
    // Degrees clockwise the hull leans, AAlpha of the way from the last
    // tick to this one
    function LeanAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    // The hatch over the well: 0 open, 1 shut
    function ShutterAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    // Where its rear wheel meets the road, its left edge at ALeft: the hull
    // leans about it
    function LeanPivot(ALeft: Single): TSdlFPoint;
    // How it stands, AAlpha of the way from the last tick to this one
    function PoseAt(AAlpha: Single): TRamPose;
    // A point of the screen where the upright hull on the road has it, moved
    // with the hull to where APose puts it
    function Posed(const APose: TRamPose; const APoint: TSdlFPoint): TSdlFPoint;
    // HullSpot of the hull standing as APose says
    function PoseSpot(const APose: TRamPose; const APoint: THullPoint): TSdlFPoint;
    // 1 as the nose meets the road, dying out as the hull settles; 0 - none
    function ScrapeLevel: Single;
    // Its honeycomb gone, the bare hull throws a bullet off and loses
    // nothing: where the stretch first meets it, and the way the face it
    // meets there looks. Nothing while the honeycomb holds - that takes
    // the bullet (Block).
    function StrikeHull(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AAt,
      ANormal: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    // The wheel it has shed throws a bullet off as the hull does
    function StrikeWheel(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AAt,
      ANormal: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    // The nozzles out under the hull throw a bullet off as the hull does:
    // they hang under it, out of the body's grid, and a shot from under
    // them would pass on into the bays
    function StrikeNozzles(const AFrom, ATo: TSdlFPoint; out AAt,
      ANormal: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    // The bare hull or its wheel threw a bullet off within ATicks
    function HullStruckWithin(ATicks: Integer): Boolean;
    // Some of AHeroBody is in the hull or a wheel: AAway - the side to set
    // him out to, as a touch would throw him; 0 - straight up
    function InTheHull(const AHeroBody: TSdlFRect; out AAway: Integer): Boolean;
    // Off the left edge, turning round: how near it is to coming back, 0
    // unseen to 1 the moment it sets off - its eye's red at the edge
    function PeekLevel: Single;
    // Turned round: bow first to the right, everything on the hull
    // mirrored
    function HullMirrored: Boolean;
    // The middle of the well on the screen, the hull's left edge at ALeft
    function WellAt(ALeft: Single): Single;
    // A point of the hull's art on the screen, the hull's left edge at ALeft
    function HullSpot(ALeft: Single; const APoint: THullPoint): TSdlFPoint;
    // On the screen to be seen and touched
    function Present: Boolean;
    // Between the last tick and this one, AAlpha of the way
    function LeftAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    function MastAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    function SwayAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    function LampsAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    function EyeAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    function LensAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    function AimAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    // How red the sweeper's barrels burn, 0 cold to 1 the sweep
    function HeatAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    // Units the hull has rolled this tick, to the right above zero
    function Rolled: Single;
    // The head's width as a share of its own: 1 but in the middle of a turn
    function TurnSquash: Single;
    // At the last third of its lives
    function Wounded: Boolean;
    // How hard the head shorts out: 0 over half its lives, from the
    // tank's floor at half up to 1 as the last of them goes
    function ShortLevel: Single;
    // The sweeper has lost its last life and backs off to the right wall
    property Retreating: Boolean read FRetreating;
    // The sweeper, at the wall, overloads and has not burst yet
    function Overloading: Boolean;
    // How far the overload has gone, 0 none to 1 the burst
    function Overload: Single;
    // The white of the sweeper's blast between two ticks, 0 none to 1 the
    // tick it bursts
    function FlashAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    property BlastAt: TSdlFPoint read FBlastAt;
    // The shock wave's front between two ticks: units from BlastAt; below
    // 0 when there is no wave
    function WaveFrontAt(AAlpha: Single): Single;
    // How far the front runs: to the farthest corner of the screen
    property WaveReach: Single read FWave.Reach;
    // The front has reached APoint by this tick
    function WaveReaches(const APoint: TSdlFPoint): Boolean;
    // The front has reached the middle of the hero's body this tick, once a
    // wave: he is thrown to AAway, with no wound, and is out of the
    // machine's way until he comes down
    function WaveStrikes(const AHeroBody: TSdlFRect;
      out AAway: Integer): Boolean;
    // The eye or the barrels were struck a moment ago
    function Hurt: Boolean;
    // The row of lives is still coming up: the target burns white
    function Booting: Boolean;
    function Row: TRamRow;
    // The middle of the top of the head, between two ticks
    function HeadTopAt(AAlpha: Single): TSdlFPoint;
    property Head: TRamHead read FHead;
    property Hatch: TBunkerHatch read FHatch;
    property HeadShield: TTekShield read FHeadShield;
    property Facing: Integer read FFacing;
    property Lives: Integer read FLives;
    property FullLives: Integer read FFullLives;
    property Pressing: Boolean read FPressing;
    // The whole entrance has begun on this level: the hero has come to the
    // fight, and a death brings him back to it
    property Entered: Boolean read FEntered;
    // The head is up and locked
    property Armed: Boolean read FArmed;
    property Fire: TRamFire read FFire;
    // The lens burns red: a burst is coming or under way
    property LensHot: Boolean read FLensHot;
    property Body: TShieldMask read FBody;
    property Shield: TTekShield read FShield;
    // The sweeper's plates, under its barrels
    function Plate(AIndex: Integer): TTekShield;
    property Phase: TRamPhase read FPhase;
    property EyeLit: Boolean read FEyeLit;
    // How bright the eye burns, 0 dark to 1 the flash of a blink
    property Eye: Single read FEye;
    // How bright the head's lens burns, 0 dark to 1 a wink
    property Lens: Single read FLens;
    // Counts the starts: a painter that sees it change knows the machine
    // came anew, and what it left in the air is gone
    property Arrivals: Integer read FArrivals;
    // The mast's height: units the socket of the head stands over the
    // middle line of the well
    property Mast: Single read FMast;
    property Left: Single read FX;
    property Track: string read FOrders.Track;
    property FlightTrack: string read FOrders.FlightTrack;
  end;

  // The art of the Ram through a cache of its own: painted with soft edges,
  // so no color key; drawn at a size of its own, so linear filtering. The
  // hull, its worn copy and the wheels are the hull art's.
  TRamArt = class
  private
    FRenderer: PSdlRenderer;
    FSpriteSet: TSpriteSet;
    FCache: TSpriteCache;
    FWell: PSdlTexture;
    FMasts: array [1..3] of PSdlTexture;
    FHunter: PSdlTexture;
    FHunterBarrel: PSdlTexture;
    FSweeper: PSdlTexture;
    FSweeperHeat: PSdlTexture;
    FBunker: PSdlTexture;
    FBunkerLid: PSdlTexture;
    FShutter: PSdlTexture;
    FBay: PSdlTexture;
    FNozzle: PSdlTexture;
    FNozzleLit: PSdlTexture;
    // The fire out of a nozzle, the mouth at its top
    FFlame: PSdlTexture;
    FHullArt: THullArt;
    FShield: TShieldArt;
    // A point of light: the brake lamps, the eye, the lens
    FGlow: PSdlTexture;
    // The dark band of the shock wave: a ring just inside the edge of its
    // square, drawn black
    FWaveBand: PSdlTexture;
    FBody: TShieldMask;
    FWells: TShieldMask;
  public
    constructor Create(ARenderer: PSdlRenderer);
    destructor Destroy; override;
    // The hull and the wheels on a grid of units, read off the art
    property Body: TShieldMask read FBody;
    // The cells of the body that are the wheels and the dark of their
    // arches, not the hull
    property Wells: TShieldMask read FWells;
  end;

  TExhaustPair = array [0..1] of TSmoke;

  TRamPainter = class
  private
    FArt: TRamArt;
    FRam: TRam;
    FHull: THull;
    // A pair for each way the hull faces, the jets thrown back off the
    // stern; the pair of the other way puffs no more and its smoke clears
    // A for-in over it walks all four smokes, both pairs
    FExhausts: array [Boolean] of TExhaustPair;
    FExhaustDriving: Boolean;
    // From a wounded head, or from the top of an empty mast
    FHeadSmoke: TSmoke;
    FHeadSmoking: Boolean;
    // The bolts over a head under half its lives, one source a head
    FShorts: array [rhHunter..rhBunker] of TLightning;
    // The bunker's column of exhaust
    FColumn: TSmoke;
    FColumnOn: Boolean;
    FAge: Integer;
    // The thick bolts of the sweeper's overload
    FOverloadShort: TLightning;
    // The dust the wave kicks up where its front runs along the road, one
    // a side of the blast
    FWaveDust: array [0..1] of TSmoke;
    // Out of the wheel arches of a stunned machine; ticks since the stun
    FArchSmoke: array [0..1] of TSmoke;
    FArchSmoking: Boolean;
    FArchSmokeTicks: Integer;
    // Off the point of its plough as its nose drops onto the road
    FScrape: TSparkField;
    FWheelSparks: TSparkField;
    // The dust a jet blows off the road while it reaches it
    FJetDust: array [TTakeoffJet] of TSmoke;
    FArrivals: Integer;
    procedure TickArrival;
    procedure TickExhausts(ABeltShift: Single);
    procedure TickHeadSmoke(ABeltShift: Single);
    procedure TickShorts;
    procedure TickColumn(ABeltShift: Single);
    procedure TickWaveDust;
    procedure TickArchSmoke(ABeltShift: Single);
    procedure TickScrape;
    procedure TickWheelSparks;
    procedure SprayStrike(const AWheel: TLooseWheel);
    procedure TickJets;
    function NozzleTop(const APose: TRamPose; AJet: TTakeoffJet): TSdlFPoint;
    function NozzleOut(const APose: TRamPose; AJet: TTakeoffJet;
      AAlpha: Single): Single;
    function NozzleMouth(const APose: TRamPose; AJet: TTakeoffJet;
      AAlpha: Single): TSdlFPoint;
    procedure DrawEngines(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer;
      const APose: TRamPose; AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawFlames(ARenderer: PSdlRenderer; AOrigin: TSdlPoint;
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawJetGlow(AOrigin: TSdlPoint; AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawLid(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AWell, AMast,
      ASway, AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawColumn(const ACanvas: TDynamicCanvas; AOrigin: TSdlPoint;
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawTop(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AWell, AMast, ASway,
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawMast(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AWell, AMast,
      ASway, AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawHead(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AWell, AMast,
      ASway, AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawShutter(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; const APose: TRamPose;
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawLamps(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; const APose: TRamPose;
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawEye(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; const APose: TRamPose;
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawPeek(AOrigin: TSdlPoint; AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawLens(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AWell, AMast, ASway,
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawHeat(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AWell, AMast, ASway,
      AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawOverload(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AWell, AMast,
      ASway: Single);
    procedure DrawFlash(AOrigin: TSdlPoint; AAlpha: Single);
    procedure DrawWave(AOrigin: TSdlPoint; AAlpha: Single);
  public
    // Both belong to the caller and must outlive the painter
    constructor Create(AArt: TRamArt; ARam: TRam);
    destructor Destroy; override;
    // After the Ram's tick: the wheels roll, the exhausts smoke.
    // ABeltShift - units the road has gone left under it this tick: the
    // wheels roll by it too, the exhausts work as in a drive, and the
    // smoke in the air rides away with the road.
    procedure Tick(ABeltShift: Single);
    // The exhausts' smoke, the jets' dust and their fire, before the body:
    // the machine backs into the smoke, the fire bursts out from under the
    // nozzles' lips
    procedure DrawSmoke(const ACanvas: TDynamicCanvas; AOrigin: TSdlPoint;
      AAlpha: Single);
    // The machine, on the world's shake channel the sprites stand at
    procedure DrawBody(const ASprites: TSpriteRenderer; AAlpha: Single);
    // The dust of the wave, the smoke out of the arches, the sparks of the
    // scrape, the glow of the jets and their warmth on the road, the bolts
    // of a head, the shield, the
    // sweeper's plates, the wave itself and the white of the blast
    procedure DrawLight(const ACanvas: TDynamicCanvas; AOrigin: TSdlPoint;
      AAlpha: Single);
    // The eye once more, over a darkness ADepth deep: the body's eye is
    // under it, and the two add up to its own light
    procedure DrawEyeOverDark(AOrigin: TSdlPoint; AAlpha, ADepth: Single);
  end;

implementation

uses
  System.SysUtils, System.Math, Render.Glow, Levels.Tint, Game.Space,
  Game.Impacts;

resourcestring
  SRamArtFailed = 'Cannot read the Ram''s body off "%s": %s';

type
  // A third of the hunter's lives: how long the lens burns before the
  // burst, how many shots and how far apart, the rest after; Lead - it
  // aims where he will be; Hose - it keeps following him through the burst
  TFirePattern = record
    FlareTicks, Shots, GapTicks, RestTicks: Integer;
    Lead, Hose: Boolean;
  end;

  THeadShape = record
    Width, Height, SocketX, SocketY: Single;
  end;

  // A third of the sweeper's lives: how long the barrels burn before the
  // sweep, how many shots and how far apart, the rest after; Fork - a
  // second sweep at once, a row over or under; Ladder - it rides the mast
  // while it sweeps
  TSweepPattern = record
    HeatTicks, Shots, GapTicks, RestTicks: Integer;
    Fork, Ladder: Boolean;
  end;

const
  FirePatterns: array [0..2] of TFirePattern = (
    (FlareTicks: 20; Shots: 3; GapTicks: 4; RestTicks: 50; Lead: False; Hose: False),
    (FlareTicks: 16; Shots: 3; GapTicks: 4; RestTicks: 40; Lead: True; Hose: False),
    (FlareTicks: 14; Shots: 6; GapTicks: 5; RestTicks: 45; Lead: False; Hose: True));

  SweepPatterns: array [0..2] of TSweepPattern = (
    (HeatTicks: 22; Shots: 8; GapTicks: 3; RestTicks: 55; Fork: False; Ladder: False),
    (HeatTicks: 18; Shots: 8; GapTicks: 3; RestTicks: 50; Fork: True; Ladder: False),
    (HeatTicks: 16; Shots: 12; GapTicks: 3; RestTicks: 50; Fork: False; Ladder: True));

  // The heads as the art draws them, facing left; the socket at the bottom
  // The bunker's art faces right: its points here are mirrored to the
  // others' left-facing frame, X = the width less the art's
  HeadShapes: array [TRamHead] of THeadShape = (
    (Width: 0; Height: 0; SocketX: 0; SocketY: 0),
    (Width: 27.7; Height: 18.8; SocketX: 16.6; SocketY: 18.7),
    (Width: 42.1; Height: 18.7; SocketX: 29.2; SocketY: 18.7),
    (Width: 28.2; Height: 34.3; SocketX: 17.9; SocketY: 34.1));

const
  LogicTicksPerSecond = 33;
  RamSetName = 'tek-machine';

  // The entrance. The hull comes in a little beyond the right edge, so its
  // rumble is heard before its ram is seen; about 3 s from the edge to the
  // stop.
  EnterFromX = ScreenWidth + 40;
  EnterSpeed = 2.8; // units a tick
  // Units a tick every tick, braking and getting up to speed alike: a
  // stop from the entrance's speed takes about 20 units
  Brake = 0.2;
  // A brake never comes to rest short of its mark
  CreepSpeed = 0.3;
  // The silence after the fade-out, before the rumble
  SilenceBeatTicks = 16;
  BreathTicks = 16;
  RiseTicks = 50;
  // From the lock to the first drive of the fight
  LockRestTicks = 33;
  EntranceStopJolt = 0.25;

  // The fight: a mark anywhere the hull fits between the walls, a leg of a
  // cell and a half at least, a rest of 1.5 to 3 s between legs; now and
  // then a leg to the far wall
  PatrolSpeed = 1.4;
  PatrolMinLeg = 48;
  WallLegShare = 1 / 3;
  PatrolRestMinTicks = 50;
  PatrolRestMaxTicks = 100;
  PatrolStopJolt = 0.12;

  // Low is where the ram can crush him: feet under the line two cells over
  // the road - the road and a jump off it, not the low pads (their decks
  // stand at 280). It presses once he has been low this long; it lets go
  // once he has stood on a pad, or kept above the line, this long.
  LowLine = RamFloorY - 64;
  PressAfterTicks = 10;
  LeaveOnDeckTicks = 6;
  LeaveAboveTicks = 33;
  // The press: a rev, then to the wall on his side a little slower than he
  // runs (2 a tick); at the last third a little faster. A short rest at the
  // wall, then it looks again.
  RevTicks = 8;
  RevJolt = 0.06;
  PressSpeeds: array [0..2] of Single = (1.9, 1.9, 2.1);
  PressRestTicks = 13;
  // The hunt: short legs that keep the hero in the barrel's sights
  HuntSpeed = 1.1;
  HuntMinLeg = 32;
  HuntMaxLeg = 96;
  HuntRestMinTicks = 15;
  HuntRestMaxTicks = 40;
  // Out of its sights it does not stand long
  HuntBlindRestTicks = 5;

  // The barrel aims within its half, from straight up to this far under
  // level; it turns this fast following the hero, and the hose of the last
  // third follows him slower through its burst
  AimBelow = 25.0;
  TrackRate = 3.0;
  HoseRate = 2.0;
  // A burst begins once the barrel is this close to where it wants to be
